Conversion to ONNX
------------------

The file is not NVIDIA's original checkpoint. It is an **ONNX export** of
NVIDIA NeMo TitaNet-small, produced by the sherpa-onnx project:

    Copyright    2024  Xiaomi Corp.        (authors: Fangjun Kuang)
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

    sherpa-onnx          https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
    Export script        https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/tree/master/scripts/nemo/speaker-verification

The export is a plain `EncDecSpeakerLabelModel.from_pretrained("titanet_small")`
followed by an ONNX export; the weights are NVIDIA's, unretrained and
unfine-tuned. The script is Apache-2.0, as is sherpa-onnx as a whole.


Changes made by this project: none
----------------------------------

Word Bank redistributes that export **byte for byte**. The file here is the
release asset `nemo_en_titanet_small.onnx` from the sherpa-onnx
`speaker-recongition-models` release (their spelling), unaltered — 40,257,283
bytes, SHA-256
`ad4a1802485d8b34c722d2a9d04249662f2ece5d28a7a039063ca22f515a789e`.
`npm run voice:verify` re-checks that from the repo, so the claim is testable
rather than asserted.

The ONNX conversion described above is therefore the only modification in the
chain, and it was made by Xiaomi Corp rather than by this project. Word Bank
has changed nothing about the model: not the weights, not the graph, not its
embedded metadata.


Why it is here, and what it does
--------------------------------

Voice Lock compares a recording made on the device against a saved voiceprint
so that only Harlie's own voice is transcribed. The model runs entirely in the
browser; no audio is uploaded and nothing is fetched at run time. See
`README.md` in this directory for provenance and measurements, and CLAUDE.md
section 18 for the decisions behind the feature.
